    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return a `selfLink` field equal to `/api/owners/` + the owner's id. I implemented it following the codebase's established idiom for derived DTO fields (a small policy class mapped via MapStruct), keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New file `OwnerSelfLinkPolicy.java`** \u2014 a small, self-contained final class with a single one-line static `selfLink(Owner)` method (CC=1, no surrounding class complexity to hold).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line to `toOwnerDto`, matching the existing pattern of the other computed fields (`ageBand`, `identityKey`, etc.). No method body changed.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `selfLink` string property on the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\nNo existing method logic was modified, so the biggest cost lever (WMC_other of a large class) is avoided \u2014 the behaviour lives in a brand-new tiny unit, and the only edited functions are the interface mapping declaration. Full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test passing).",
